-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part snap1 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for the seat layer of part snap1: at least one case per question, with the facts a household member would state.
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the Act (7 U.S.C. 2012a to 2014a, 2018(j)) and, for the income standards, the standard deduction,
-- the shelter cap and the resource limits, the USDA's FY2027 figures that the rules hold as data. None is copied from a run.
-- Inputs are given in the order the question asks them. JUST FALSE is asserted only where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING is the text not deciding the case.


-- Under section 2012a
-- 2012a: the provision of section 2019 reaches a publicly operated community health center only where it concerns private nonprofit drug or alcohol programs.
#ASSERT `Under section 2012a, does section 2019 also apply to the publicly operated community health center I use` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not covered: not a publicly operated center
#ASSERT `Under section 2012a, does section 2019 also apply to the publicly operated community health center I use` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not covered: the rule is not about private nonprofit drug or alcohol programs
#ASSERT `Under section 2012a, does section 2019 also apply to the publicly operated community health center I use` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 2013
#ASSERT `Under section 2013(a)(1), is my household given the opportunity to receive an allotment` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
