-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part snap3 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- CASES for the seat layer (snap3-seat.l4): a member of a household that applies for, or receives, SNAP benefits.
-- Each case is a person's own facts and the answer worked out from the text of the Act, written BEFORE running.
-- JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not say (never read it as "no").
-- The arguments of a question follow its GIVEN list in snap3-seat.l4.

§ `Cases -- Under section 2016`

-- Under section 2016(a): certified household, card not under the State option. The text limits who gets a card; it does not itself say a certified household gets one.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(a), may an EBT card be issued to my household` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A household not certified as eligible, card not under the State option: the text says "only to households which have been duly certified".
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(a), may an EBT card be issued to my household` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Under the State option in subsection (i): the text sends the question to subsection (i).
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(a), may an EBT card be issued to my household` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 2016(b): food, from an approved store, at the usual price.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(b), may I use my benefits for this purchase` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not food: the text says "only to purchase food".
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(b), may I use my benefits for this purchase` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A store not approved for SNAP.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(b), may I use my benefits for this purchase` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A price above the store's usual price.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(b), may I use my benefits for this purchase` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 2016(k)(2)(B): a delivery fee on an online order cannot be paid with benefits; a charge that is not such a fee is not covered by this rule.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(k)(2)(B), may I use my benefits to pay a fee on an online food order` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(k)(2)(B), may I use my benefits to pay a fee on an online food order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 2016(g)(2)(A)(ii): 40 days between issuances is allowed, 41 is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(g)(2)(A)(ii), is the wait between my issuances within the 40-day limit` 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(g)(2)(A)(ii), is the wait between my issuances within the 40-day limit` 41 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 2016(h)(8): replacement cards.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(8)(A), may my State agency charge me for a replacement card by reducing my allotment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A card that is not a replacement: the paragraph is silent.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(8)(A), may my State agency charge me for a replacement card by reducing my allotment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Excessive requests and no explanation: the Secretary may require the State agency to refuse another card.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(8)(B)(i), may the State agency be required to refuse me another replacement card` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Excessive requests but the household explained the loss: "unless the household ... provides an explanation".
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(8)(B)(i), may the State agency be required to refuse me another replacement card` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No excessive requests: the power depends on "if a household makes excessive requests".
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(8)(B)(i), may the State agency be required to refuse me another replacement card` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Held back until the household meets the requirements: "nothing in this paragraph shall be considered a denial of ... eligibility".
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(8)(D), does being refused a replacement card count as a denial of my eligibility` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(8)(D), does being refused a replacement card count as a denial of my eligibility` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 2016(h)(12): stored and unused benefits.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(II), did the State agency make my stored benefits available in time` 48 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(II), did the State agency make my stored benefits available in time` 49 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Benefits to be expunged on 31 January 2026: the last day for notice is 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I), was my notice that my unused benefits would be expunged given in time` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I), was my notice that my unused benefits would be expunged given in time` TRUE (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A notice that does not say benefits will be expunged and when is not "sufficient notice".
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I), was my notice that my unused benefits would be expunged given in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 2016(h)(13): fees.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(13)(A), does an interchange fee apply to my EBT transaction` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(13)(A), does an interchange fee apply to my EBT transaction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A switching fee charged by a State on the last day of fiscal year 2023: barred. The next day: the text is silent about later years.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(13)(B), may a State or its contractor charge a fee for switching or routing my benefits` (Date 30 9 2023) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(h)(13)(B), may a State or its contractor charge a fee for switching or routing my benefits` (Date 1 10 2023) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 2016(i)(1): the State option.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(i)(1), may my State issue me benefits although I am ineligible for the reason the subsection names` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(i)(1), may my State issue me benefits although I am ineligible for the reason the subsection names` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2016(i)(1), may my State issue me benefits although I am ineligible for the reason the subsection names` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Cases -- Under section 2016a`

-- Under section 2016a(b)(2): arguments are the State agency decided it was theft, the date stolen, the amount stolen, the monthly allotment before the theft, replacements already made this fiscal year.
-- $500 stolen, two months of a $300 allotment is $600: the lesser, $500.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016a(b)(2), up to how many dollars of my stolen benefits must be replaced` TRUE (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 0 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `Under section 2016a(b)(2), does the text rule out replacing my stolen benefits` TRUE (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- $800 stolen: capped at two months of the allotment, $600.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016a(b)(2), up to how many dollars of my stolen benefits must be replaced` TRUE (Date 15 3 2023) 800 300 0 EQUALS JUST 600
-- Stolen on 21 December 2024, the day after the period ends: the text says "only to benefits stolen during the period".
#ASSERT `Under section 2016a(b)(2), up to how many dollars of my stolen benefits must be replaced` TRUE (Date 21 12 2024) 500 300 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2016a(b)(2), does the text rule out replacing my stolen benefits` TRUE (Date 21 12 2024) 500 300 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Stolen on the first day of the period, 1 October 2022: inside.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016a(b)(2), up to how many dollars of my stolen benefits must be replaced` TRUE (Date 1 10 2022) 500 300 0 EQUALS JUST 500
-- A third replacement in the fiscal year: "shall not occur more than 2 times per Federal fiscal year".
#ASSERT `Under section 2016a(b)(2), does the text rule out replacing my stolen benefits` TRUE (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The State agency has not decided the benefits were stolen by skimming: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 2016a(b)(2), up to how many dollars of my stolen benefits must be replaced` FALSE (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2016a(b)(2), does the text rule out replacing my stolen benefits` FALSE (Date 15 3 2023) 500 300 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Cases -- Under section 2017`

-- Under section 2017(a), fiscal year 2027. A household of 3 in the 48 States: cost 808, less 30 per cent of net income 500 (150) is 658.
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(a), what is my household's monthly allotment, fiscal year 2027` TRUE 3 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 500 EQUALS JUST 658
-- A household of 1 with net income $1,000: 306 less 300 is 6, below the minimum allotment of 25.
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(a), what is my household's monthly allotment, fiscal year 2027` TRUE 1 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 1000 EQUALS JUST 25
-- A household of 2 in Hawaii with no income: cost 910.
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(a), what is my household's monthly allotment, fiscal year 2027` TRUE 2 Hawaii 0 EQUALS JUST 910
-- A household of 10 in the 48 States, net income 1000: the 8-member total 1841 plus 2 x 225 is 2291, less 300 is 1991.
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(a), what is my household's monthly allotment, fiscal year 2027` TRUE 10 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 1000 EQUALS JUST 1991
-- A household of 4 whose reduced cost would be below zero (1023 less 1050): the text gives no value.
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(a), what is my household's monthly allotment, fiscal year 2027` TRUE 4 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 3500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not certified as eligible: the section speaks of "households certified as eligible".
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(a), what is my household's monthly allotment, fiscal year 2027` FALSE 3 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- No people in the household: the table has no row for it.
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(a), what is my household's monthly allotment, fiscal year 2027` TRUE 0 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 500 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 2017(b).
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(b), may a State or local body reduce other assistance I get because I receive SNAP benefits` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(b), may a State or local body reduce other assistance I get because I receive SNAP benefits` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 2017(c)(1): a full-month allotment of 400, applied on 11 January 2026: 21 of the 31 days remain, so 400 x 21 / 31.
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(c)(1), what is the value of my first-month allotment` 400 (Date 11 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (400 TIMES 21 DIVIDED BY 31)
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(c)(1), is my first-month allotment barred because it would be less than $10` 400 (Date 11 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A full-month 20, applied on the last day: 20 / 31 is under $10, so no allotment may be issued.
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(c)(1), is my first-month allotment barred because it would be less than $10` 20 (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(c)(1), what is the value of my first-month allotment` 20 (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An application date outside the month: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(c)(1), what is the value of my first-month allotment` 400 (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(c)(1), is my first-month allotment barred because it would be less than $10` 400 (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 2017(d)(1)(B): a $400 allotment may be cut by 25 percent, $100.
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(d)(1)(B), what is the most my State may cut my SNAP allotment because another programme cut my benefits` TRUE 400 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `Under section 2017(d)(1)(B), what is the most my State may cut my SNAP allotment because another programme cut my benefits` FALSE 400 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Cases -- Under section 2022`

#ASSERT `Under section 2022(a)(4), am I jointly and severally liable for the value of an overissuance to my household` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A child member: the text says "Each adult member".
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(a)(4), am I jointly and severally liable for the value of an overissuance to my household` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under section 2022(b)(3): arguments are a member found ineligible for fraud, the State collects by cutting the allotment, the monthly allotment (and the cut).
-- 10 percent of $400 is $40, more than $10.
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(b)(3), what is the most my State may cut my monthly allotment each month to collect an overissuance` FALSE TRUE 400 EQUALS JUST 40
-- 10 percent of $50 is $5, less than $10: the greater is $10.
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(b)(3), what is the most my State may cut my monthly allotment each month to collect an overissuance` FALSE TRUE 50 EQUALS JUST 10
-- A member was found ineligible for fraud: this cap does not speak to it.
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(b)(3), what is the most my State may cut my monthly allotment each month to collect an overissuance` TRUE TRUE 400 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(b)(3), may my State cut my monthly allotment by this amount to collect an overissuance` FALSE TRUE 400 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(b)(3), may my State cut my monthly allotment by this amount to collect an overissuance` FALSE TRUE 400 41 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Under section 2022(c)(3): arguments are receiving unemployment compensation and the agency checked, an agreement, a copy sent, a garnishment order.
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(c)(3), may my State recover an uncollected overissuance from my unemployment compensation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(c)(3), may my State recover an uncollected overissuance from my unemployment compensation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(c)(3), may my State recover an uncollected overissuance from my unemployment compensation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(c)(3), may my State recover an uncollected overissuance from my unemployment compensation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under section 2022(d): a $100 overissuance, recovery from a Federal tax refund authorized by section 3720A of title 31.
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(d), may an unrecovered overissuance be recovered from my Federal income tax refund` 100 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(d), may an unrecovered overissuance be recovered from my Federal income tax refund` 100 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2022(d), may an unrecovered overissuance be recovered from my Federal income tax refund` 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Cases -- Under section 2023`

-- Under section 2023(b): arguments are the date the case began, the case reviews a final State decision, asked the State, the date asked, the State knew, the date it knew.
-- Only the commencement limit: one year before 15 June 2026 is 15 June 2025.
#ASSERT `Under section 2023(b), what is the earliest date from which my wrongly withheld allotments can be restored` (Date 15 6 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 15 6 2025
-- A review of a final State decision after a request on 1 March 2026: one year before is 1 March 2025.
#ASSERT `Under section 2023(b), what is the earliest date from which my wrongly withheld allotments can be restored` (Date 15 6 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
-- The State found out about the loss on 1 January 2025: one year before is 1 January 2024.
#ASSERT `Under section 2023(b), what is the earliest date from which my wrongly withheld allotments can be restored` (Date 15 6 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS Date 1 1 2024
-- The period test: arguments as above, then the first day of the period.
#ASSERT `Under section 2023(b), can allotments be restored for a period starting on this date` (Date 15 6 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2023(b), can allotments be restored for a period starting on this date` (Date 15 6 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 14 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Cases -- Under section 2024`

-- Under section 2024(b)(1): arguments are the value of the benefits, this would be a second or later conviction.
-- $5,000: a felony, fine up to $250,000, up to 20 years, nothing required.
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), is knowingly misusing benefits of this value a felony` 5000 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the most the fine may be for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` 5000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 250000
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the longest prison term, in years, for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` 5000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the shortest prison term, in years, the court must impose for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` 5000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- $4,999.99, second conviction: a felony, fine up to $10,000, between six months and five years.
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), is knowingly misusing benefits of this value a felony` 4999.99 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the most the fine may be for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` 4999.99 TRUE EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the longest prison term, in years, for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` 4999.99 TRUE EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the shortest prison term, in years, the court must impose for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` 4999.99 TRUE EQUALS JUST 0.5
-- $99.99, first conviction: a misdemeanor, fine up to $1,000, up to one year.
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), is knowingly misusing benefits of this value a felony` 99.99 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the most the fine may be for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` 99.99 FALSE EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the longest prison term, in years, for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` 99.99 FALSE EQUALS JUST 1
-- $100 exactly: "$100 or more", a felony.
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), is knowingly misusing benefits of this value a felony` 100 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A value below zero is not a value of benefits.
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), is knowingly misusing benefits of this value a felony` (0 MINUS 1) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Suspension: up to eighteen months more; arguments are convicted, the months asked.
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), may the court also suspend me from SNAP for this many more months` TRUE 18 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), may the court also suspend me from SNAP for this many more months` TRUE 19 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(1), may the court also suspend me from SNAP for this many more months` FALSE 18 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(2), may the court let me do work for restitution instead of being sentenced now` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(b)(2), may the court let me do work for restitution instead of being sentenced now` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under section 2024(c): $100 or more is a felony, fine up to $20,000; less is a misdemeanor, fine up to $1,000.
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(c), is knowingly presenting benefits for redemption in violation of the Act, worth this much, a felony` 100 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(c), what is the most the fine may be for presenting benefits of this value for redemption in violation of the Act` 100 FALSE EQUALS JUST 20000
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(c), is knowingly presenting benefits for redemption in violation of the Act, worth this much, a felony` 99.99 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(c), what is the most the fine may be for presenting benefits of this value for redemption in violation of the Act` 99.99 FALSE EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(c), what is the most the fine may be for presenting benefits of this value for redemption in violation of the Act` (0 MINUS 1) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under section 2024(e) and (f)(3).
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(e), may the Secretary subject to forfeiture what was given in exchange for benefits` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(e), may the Secretary subject to forfeiture what was given in exchange for benefits` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(f)(3), can my interest in property be forfeited for an act I did not know about or agree to` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2024(f)(3), can my interest in property be forfeited for an act I did not know about or agree to` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part snap4 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for snap4-seat.l4: a member of a household that applies for, or receives, SNAP benefits.
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section the question cites BEFORE running; none is copied from the encoding's output.
-- JUST TRUE is the text's yes, JUST FALSE the text's own no, NOTHING "not covered". A caller must never read NOTHING as no.
-- Each question has at least one case with the facts a real person in the seat would state, and the questions whose module can return NOTHING have a "not covered" case.

§ `cases -- who runs the program (section 2020(a) to (d))`

-- Maria lives in a State that takes part in SNAP: the State agency certifies her household and issues the EBT cards (2020(a)(1)).
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(a)(1), is the State agency the one that certifies my household and issues our EBT cards` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A State that does not take part: the text says nothing.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(a)(1), is the State agency the one that certifies my household and issues our EBT cards` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Her county runs the program: the text says the State agency's responsibility is not affected (2020(a)(2)); some other basis is not spoken of.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(a)(2), does it change the State agency's responsibility for my case that my county, not the State, runs the program` `s 2020(a)(2) county-administered` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(a)(2), does it change the State agency's responsibility for my case that my county, not the State, runs the program` `s 2020(a)(2) State-administered` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(a)(2), does it change the State agency's responsibility for my case that my county, not the State, runs the program` `s 2020(a)(2) administered on some other basis` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The State agency learns it wrongly denied an eligible household: it must promptly restore the benefits (2020(b)); with no such finding the text is silent.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(b), must the State agency promptly restore benefits it wrongly denied my household` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(b), must the State agency promptly restore benefits it wrongly denied my household` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Discrimination on a named ground is barred (2020(c)(1)); a ground that is not named is not spoken of.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(c)(1), may the State agency treat my household differently when certifying us because of race, sex, religious creed, national origin or political affiliation` `s 2020(c)(1) national origin` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(c)(1), may the State agency treat my household differently when certifying us because of race, sex, religious creed, national origin or political affiliation` `s 2020(c)(1) political affiliation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(c)(1), may the State agency treat my household differently when certifying us because of race, sex, religious creed, national origin or political affiliation` `s 2020(c)(1) some other ground` EQUALS NOTHING

-- A reservation (2020(d)). Arguments: the Secretary decided on the State agency; found it failing; decided on the tribal organization; found it capable.
-- Both decisions made and both found: the tribal organization runs it.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(d), is a tribal organization, not the State agency, the one that runs SNAP on my reservation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Secretary found the State agency not failing: the State agency stays responsible.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(d), is a tribal organization, not the State agency, the one that runs SNAP on my reservation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Secretary found the tribal organization not capable: the State agency stays responsible.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(d), is a tribal organization, not the State agency, the one that runs SNAP on my reservation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Only the first decision made: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(d), is a tribal organization, not the State agency, the one that runs SNAP on my reservation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No decision at all: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(d), is a tribal organization, not the State agency, the one that runs SNAP on my reservation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `cases -- applying and being certified (section 2020(e)(1) to (5))`

-- The State agency has chosen to run outreach (2020(e)(1)(A)): it must tell low-income households about the program.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(1)(A), must the State agency tell low-income households about SNAP, how to apply and what it pays` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(1)(A), must the State agency tell low-income households about SNAP, how to apply and what it pays` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Rosa walks into the SNAP office for the first time, during office hours: she may apply that day (2020(e)(2)(B)(iii)).
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(2)(B)(iii), may my household apply on the same day we first go to a SNAP office` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside office hours the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(2)(B)(iii), may my household apply on the same day we first go to a SNAP office` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- An application with name, address and signature, handed in on 5 March 2026, is filed that day (2020(e)(2)(B)(iv)).
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(2)(B)(iv), on what day does my application count as filed` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 3 2026)
-- Unsigned: the text does not say it is filed.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(2)(B)(iv), on what day does my application count as filed` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- An eligible household is entitled to certification and a retroactive allotment within thirty days of filing (2020(e)(3)).
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(3), is my household entitled to be certified, with a retroactive allotment, within thirty days after we filed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(3), is my household entitled to be certified, with a retroactive allotment, within thirty days after we filed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Filed 1 March 2026, certified 31 March 2026: the thirtieth day, in time. Certified 1 April 2026: the thirty-first day, too late.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(3), did the State agency certify us and provide our allotment within thirty days after we filed` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`Under section 2020(e)(3), did the State agency certify us and provide our allotment within thirty days after we filed` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026))

-- Recertification (2020(e)(4)): still eligible and filed in time, so the next allotment comes within a month of the last.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(4), am I entitled to my next allotment within one month after my last, if I am recertified` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(4), am I entitled to my next allotment within one month after my last, if I am recertified` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Found ineligible or eligible for less in the new period: no benefits on the old certification pending a hearing.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(4), do we keep getting benefits on the old certification while a fair hearing is pending, if the new period finds us ineligible or eligible for less` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(4), do we keep getting benefits on the old certification while a fair hearing is pending, if the new period finds us ineligible or eligible for less` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- An additional requirement beyond sections 2014 and 2015 may not be imposed (2020(e)(5)).
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(5), may the State agency add its own requirement, beyond those in sections 2014 and 2015, when deciding whether I am eligible` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(5), may the State agency add its own requirement, beyond those in sections 2014 and 2015, when deciding whether I am eligible` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `cases -- acting for you and keeping your information private (section 2020(e)(7) and (8))`

-- A designated adult who knows the household may help with the certification process, absent a Secretary restriction (2020(e)(7)).
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(7), may a person who is not in my household act for us` `s 2020(e)(7) the certification process` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not designated by the head or spouse: no, for buying food.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(7), may a person who is not in my household act for us` `s 2020(e)(7) food purchase` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A Secretary restriction bars it: the text leaves the case to the Secretary.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(7), may a person who is not in my household act for us` `s 2020(e)(7) the certification process` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Use for a purpose the paragraph does not list: the safeguards must prohibit it (2020(e)(8)).
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(8), must the State agency's safeguards stop it from using or sharing what I told it on my application for this purpose` `s 2020(e)(8) any other use or disclosure` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A listed purpose with its conditions met (here, a law-enforcement request to investigate a violation): not prohibited.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(8), must the State agency's safeguards stop it from using or sharing what I told it on my application for this purpose` `s 2020(e)(8)(C) disclosure on request to local, State or Federal law enforcement officials to investigate an alleged violation of this chapter or a regulation under it` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same purpose with the conditions not met: the safeguards must prohibit it.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(8), must the State agency's safeguards stop it from using or sharing what I told it on my application for this purpose` `s 2020(e)(8)(C) disclosure on request to local, State or Federal law enforcement officials to investigate an alleged violation of this chapter or a regulation under it` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `cases -- getting benefits quickly, hearings and lost benefits (section 2020(e)(9) to (11))`

-- Expedited service, (A): income $149 a month and $100 in the bank: benefits within seven days.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(9)(A), is my household entitled to benefits within seven days after we apply, because we have very little income and money` 149 FALSE 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Income of $150 and no migrant status: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(9)(A), is my household entitled to benefits within seven days after we apply, because we have very little income and money` 150 FALSE 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A destitute migrant household with $500 income and $100 in the bank: seven days.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(9)(A), is my household entitled to benefits within seven days after we apply, because we have very little income and money` 500 TRUE 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (B): income $100 plus $50 in the bank, rent and utilities $151: more outgoings than means, so seven days. Rent $150: not more, so the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(9)(B), is my household entitled to benefits within seven days after we apply, because our rent and utilities are more than our income and money` 100 50 151 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(9)(B), is my household entitled to benefits within seven days after we apply, because our rent and utilities are more than our income and money` 100 50 150 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Applied 1 March 2026: benefits on 8 March are the seventh day, in time; on 9 March they are late.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(9), did we receive our benefits within seven days after we applied` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 8 3 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`Under section 2020(e)(9), did we receive our benefits within seven days after we applied` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026))

-- A household aggrieved by the State agency's action is entitled to a fair hearing (2020(e)(10)); aggrieved by neither, the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(10), am I entitled to a fair hearing and a prompt decision after it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(10), am I entitled to a fair hearing and a prompt decision after it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(10), am I entitled to a fair hearing and a prompt decision after it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A timely hearing request, no adverse decision yet, certification period still running: benefits continue.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(10), do we keep getting the benefits we were getting while we wait for the hearing` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Hearing decided against the household: benefits do not continue.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(10), do we keep getting the benefits we were getting while we wait for the hearing` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No request for a hearing at all: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(10), do we keep getting the benefits we were getting while we wait for the hearing` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Wrongly denied benefits (2020(e)(11)): asked for, wrongly denied, loss starting 1 March 2025 and noticed 1 March 2026 is exactly one year: restored.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(11), must the State agency restore benefits for the period we lost them` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A loss starting 28 February 2025, more than one year before the State agency learned of it on 1 March 2026: not restored.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(11), must the State agency restore benefits for the period we lost them` TRUE TRUE (Date 28 2 2025) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No request: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(e)(11), must the State agency restore benefits for the period we lost them` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `cases -- transitional benefits (section 2020(s))`

-- Cash assistance ended 15 January 2026: 16 January and 15 June 2026 are within five months; 16 June is not; 15 January itself is not "after" it.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(s)(2), may my household still receive transitional benefits on a given day after our cash assistance ended` (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 16 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(s)(2), may my household still receive transitional benefits on a given day after our cash assistance ended` (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(s)(2), may my household still receive transitional benefits on a given day after our cash assistance ended` (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 16 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(s)(2), may my household still receive transitional benefits on a given day after our cash assistance ended` (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Last allotment $300; the loss of cash assistance cuts it by $100; the State agency also counts another program, cutting it by $20 more: $180.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(s)(3), how much are my household's transitional benefits each month, in dollars` 300 (0 MINUS 100) TRUE (0 MINUS 20) EQUALS 180
-- Last allotment $300; the loss of cash assistance raises it by $50; no other program: $350.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(s)(3), how much are my household's transitional benefits each month, in dollars` 300 50 FALSE 0 EQUALS 350
-- Sanctioned for failing the cash assistance program's requirements: not eligible for transitional benefits.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(s)(5), is my household eligible for transitional benefits` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(s)(5), is my household eligible for transitional benefits` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- None of the three bars: the text does not say that the household is eligible.
#ASSERT `Under section 2020(s)(5), is my household eligible for transitional benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

