-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part snap6 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- CASES for snap6-seat.l4: a member of a household that applies for or receives SNAP.
-- Every expected value is written here from the text of the section the question names, before the seat was run.
-- JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not cover the case.
-- Each question has at least one realistic case and one "not covered" case; the figures are a household's own.


§ `Cases for a SNAP household member`

§§ `Section 2026`
-- Maria's household gets $20 a month and chooses a $60 aggregate allotment covering 3 months: s 2026(a)(2) allows it.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household receive an aggregate allotment` 20 TRUE 60 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same, but the allotment would be $61: "not to exceed $60", the text says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household receive an aggregate allotment` 20 TRUE 61 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Covering 4 months: "not more than 3 months' benefits", the text says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household receive an aggregate allotment` 20 TRUE 60 4 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Monthly benefits of $25: the permission is for households whose benefits do not exceed $20, so the text does not cover it.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household receive an aggregate allotment` 25 TRUE 60 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not at the household's option: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household receive an aggregate allotment` 20 FALSE 60 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Verification not yet complied with: "no household shall begin to receive combined allotments ... until it has complied", the text says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household begin to receive combined allotments` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Verification complied with: the bar is lifted and the paragraph grants nothing here.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household begin to receive combined allotments` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Verification not decided: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household begin to receive combined allotments` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- The first aggregate allotment 40 days after the last issuance is in time; 41 days is not; a later one is not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), was my first aggregate allotment provided in time` TRUE 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), was my first aggregate allotment provided in time` TRUE 41 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(a)(2), was my first aggregate allotment provided in time` FALSE 99 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A pilot project that cuts benefits by more than 20 percent for 6 percent of the households in the area: the limits apply; for 5 percent they do not.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii), do the limits on a pilot project apply to the project in my area` 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii), do the limits on a pilot project apply to the project in my area` 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A cash project may include a household all of whose members are 65 or over; with no such member it is not covered; a privacy-respecting identification mechanism is included for anyone.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(v), may the project include this kind of change for my household` `s 2026 payment of the value of allotments, or the average value by household size, in cash to eligible households` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(v), may the project include this kind of change for my household` `s 2026 payment of the value of allotments, or the average value by household size, in cash to eligible households` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(v), may the project include this kind of change for my household` `s 2026 the use of identification mechanisms that do not invade a household's privacy` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(v), may the project include this kind of change for my household` `s 2026 some other project` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The 1981 cash project is continued if the State asks and appropriations are available; not if the State does not ask; not covered if appropriations are not shown.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi), must the cash-payment project I receive be continued` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi), must the cash-payment project I receive be continued` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi), must the cash-payment project I receive be continued` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi), must the cash-payment project I receive be continued` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A waiver approved on 1 January 1991, no EBT card, no compensation for the sales tax, the State agency paying: "No waiver ... shall be approved ... unless", the text says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(C), may the waiver or demonstration program that covers my household be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The allotment is increased to compensate and the State agency pays: the bar is lifted, the paragraph grants nothing.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(C), may the waiver or demonstration program that covers my household be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The State agency does not pay the cost: the text says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(C), may the waiver or demonstration program that covers my household be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Approved on or before 28 November 1990: the bar is "after November 28, 1990", so not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(C), may the waiver or demonstration program that covers my household be approved` (Date 28 11 1990) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Where the project already gives more than the sales tax, clause (i) does not apply: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(C), may the waiver or demonstration program that covers my household be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A waiver request the Secretary has not answered, with no prohibition: considered approved. Answered, or prohibited: the text says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii), is the waiver my State asked for considered approved` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii), is the waiver my State asked for considered approved` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii), is the waiver my State asked for considered approved` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An activity that converts benefits to cash "shall occur only with the consent of the participant": no consent, the text says no; with consent, nothing is granted; not such an activity, not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(2)(D), may I take part in an employment and training activity that converts my benefits to cash` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(2)(D), may I take part in an employment and training activity that converts my benefits to cash` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(b)(2)(D), may I take part in an employment and training activity that converts my benefits to cash` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A household on cash benefits "shall not receive any other" SNAP benefits for the period: the text says no; one not on cash benefits is not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(d)(2)(C)(ii), may my household receive other SNAP benefits for the period my cash benefits cover` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(d)(2)(C)(ii), may my household receive other SNAP benefits for the period my cash benefits cover` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(d)(2)(C)(ii), may my household receive other SNAP benefits for the period my cash benefits cover` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A sales tax may be collected and the Secretary has not found the increase unnecessary: the State shall increase the cash benefits. If the Secretary did: the text says no. No sales tax: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(d)(2)(D)(i), must my State increase my cash benefits for the sales tax` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(d)(2)(D)(i), must my State increase my cash benefits for the sales tax` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(d)(2)(D)(i), must my State increase my cash benefits for the sales tax` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An adult member who worked 90 days, earned $350 a month, is on part A benefits, still earns $350 and elects cash: eligible. At 89 days: the text says no (the "if" fails).
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(d)(3), is my household eligible to receive cash benefits through an adult member` 90 350 TRUE FALSE FALSE 350 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(d)(3), is my household eligible to receive cash benefits through an adult member` 89 350 TRUE FALSE FALSE 350 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not on part A now, but was when first receiving cash benefits and lost them to earned income: still eligible under (C)(ii).
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(d)(3), is my household eligible to receive cash benefits through an adult member` 90 350 FALSE TRUE TRUE 350 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One vehicle worth $6,000 with no listed use: $1,500 over $4,500 counts. The same vehicle used to get to work: excluded, 0. A $20,000 vehicle that is the household's home: 0.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(h), how much of the value of my vehicle counts as a financial resource` 6000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(h), how much of the value of my vehicle counts as a financial resource` 6000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(h), how much of the value of my vehicle counts as a financial resource` 20000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(h), how much of the value of my vehicle counts as a financial resource` 4000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Accumulated resources up to $10,000 are excluded: $9,999 all; $25,000 only $10,000.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(i), how much of the resources I have accumulated is excluded as a resource` 9999 EQUALS 9999
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(i), how much of the resources I have accumulated is excluded as a resource` 25000 EQUALS 10000
-- Saving for the purchase of a home is a purpose the projects test; some other purpose is not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(i), is the purpose I am saving for one the project tests` `s 2026 the purchase of a home for the household` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(i), is the purpose I am saving for one the project tests` `s 2026 some other purpose of expenditure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Income at 185 percent of the poverty level is in the target audience; at 186 percent it is not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(k)(2)(C)(i), is my household in the low-income target audience` 185 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(k)(2)(C)(i), is my household in the low-income target audience` 186 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A database that includes the member's social security number does not protect privacy: the text says no. One that does not include it does.
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(n)(4)(B)(i), does my State's longitudinal database protect my privacy` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2026(n)(4)(B)(i), does my State's longitudinal database protect my privacy` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 2031`
-- A family that takes part in the Project and is neither assigned nor required to apply: the paragraph's only limbs are the two ways; with only the first the text says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(2), may my family receive SNAP benefits` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(2), may my family receive SNAP benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Assistance of $100 against $100 under SNAP and part A: enough. $99: the text says no. With a $10 reduction, $90 is enough and $89 is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(A), is the value of the assistance my family gets under the Project enough` 100 100 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(A), is the value of the assistance my family gets under the Project enough` 99 100 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(A), is the value of the assistance my family gets under the Project enough` 90 100 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(A), is the value of the assistance my family gets under the Project enough` 89 100 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where there is a sales tax on food the State shall increase the assistance; where there is none, the text says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv), must the State increase my family's assistance for the sales tax` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv), must the State increase my family's assistance for the sales tax` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An ineligible member of a household with a participating family: 75 percent of a $100 SNAP amount is $75; 75 percent of $13 is below $10, so $10; of $15 is $11.25, rounded down $11.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv), what is my monthly allotment if I am ineligible for the Project but live with a participating family` TRUE (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 75
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv), what is my monthly allotment if I am ineligible for the Project but live with a participating family` TRUE (JUST 13) EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv), what is my monthly allotment if I am ineligible for the Project but live with a participating family` TRUE (JUST 15) EQUALS JUST 11
-- The SNAP amount not worked out: not covered. Not ineligible for the Project: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv), what is my monthly allotment if I am ineligible for the Project but live with a participating family` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv), what is my monthly allotment if I am ineligible for the Project but live with a participating family` FALSE (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Selected by application: assistance within 30 days is in time; 31 days is not; not yet issued and within 30 days is not covered; selected by assignment is not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(6)(A), did the State determine my family's eligibility and issue assistance in time` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` TRUE 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(6)(A), did the State determine my family's eligibility and issue assistance in time` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` TRUE 31 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(6)(A), did the State determine my family's eligibility and issue assistance in time` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` FALSE 10 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(6)(A), did the State determine my family's eligibility and issue assistance in time` `s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE 10 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Selected by application and entitled to expedited service: expedited benefits shall be provided. Not entitled: not covered. Selected by assignment: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(6)(C), must expedited benefits be provided to my family` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(6)(C), must expedited benefits be provided to my family` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(6)(C), must expedited benefits be provided to my family` `s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Assistance of $300 and SNAP benefits of $120 for the same period: $180 is left. SNAP benefits above the assistance: nothing is left (fork FR-31-3).
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(9), how much assistance is left after the reduction for SNAP benefits I received` 300 120 EQUALS 180
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(9), how much assistance is left after the reduction for SNAP benefits I received` 100 120 EQUALS 0
-- Participation ended and the State gave the notice: the text says yes. Ended and not given: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(10)(A), has the State given me the notice about SNAP that I am owed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(10)(A), has the State given me the notice about SNAP that I am owed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Found ineligible because of income, and eligible for SNAP: the State shall ensure benefits. Not eligible for SNAP: the text says no. Not decided: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(10)(B)(i), must the State ensure that I get SNAP benefits after I leave the Project` `s 2031 the family or member is determined ineligible for the Project because of income` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(10)(B)(i), must the State ensure that I get SNAP benefits after I leave the Project` `s 2031 the family or member is determined ineligible for the Project because of income` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(10)(B)(i), must the State ensure that I get SNAP benefits after I leave the Project` `s 2031 the Project is terminated` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(10)(B)(i), must the State ensure that I get SNAP benefits after I leave the Project` `s 2031 some other reason` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Supplied after 10 days, determined 5 days later: in time. Determined 6 days later: the text says no. Not yet determined, 5 days: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(10)(C), did the State determine my family's SNAP eligibility in time` TRUE 10 TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(10)(C), did the State determine my family's SNAP eligibility in time` TRUE 10 TRUE 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(10)(C), did the State determine my family's SNAP eligibility in time` TRUE 10 FALSE 5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A hearing is available and the family was given notice consistent with the regulations: notice as the text requires. Inconsistent: the text says no. Not decided: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(11), was my family given notice as the text requires` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(11), was my family given notice as the text requires` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(b)(11), was my family given notice as the text requires` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- A one-parent family, parent 30, well, not needed at home, youngest child 120 months, not personally caring, 10 hours, verifiable at 10 hours, earning nothing: the State may require. A parent who is ill: the text says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(c)(1), may the State require me, as a parent, to take part in education, employment or training` TRUE FALSE 30 FALSE 120 TRUE 10 TRUE 10 0 0 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(c)(1), may the State require me, as a parent, to take part in education, employment or training` TRUE TRUE 30 FALSE 120 TRUE 10 TRUE 10 0 0 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A parent whose youngest child is 11 months old and who personally cares for the child: the text says no.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(c)(1), may the State require me, as a parent, to take part in education, employment or training` TRUE FALSE 30 FALSE 11 TRUE 10 TRUE 10 0 0 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Failing a required activity without good cause, with $500 of assistance otherwise: the most the reduction may be is $50; a reduction of $50 is allowed; $50.01 is not; no failure: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(c)(3), what is the most my family's assistance may be reduced by` TRUE TRUE 500 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(c)(3), what is the most my family's assistance may be reduced by` TRUE FALSE 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(c)(3), may my family's assistance be reduced by this amount` TRUE TRUE 500 50 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(c)(3), may my family's assistance be reduced by this amount` TRUE TRUE 500 50.01 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Two children who are siblings living with a natural parent are a family; two siblings alone are not covered; a pregnant woman in the third trimester with no children is a family.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(j)(1), is my group a family for the Project` TRUE 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(j)(1), is my group a family for the Project` TRUE 2 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A group of one pregnant woman in the third trimester with no children is a family.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(j)(1), is my group a family for the Project` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A grandfather living in the home and caring for the child, no parent in the home, asked to determine eligibility: a caregiver. With a parent in the home: the text says no. A natural parent living there: a caregiver.
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(j)(3), am I a caregiver of the minor child` `s 2031 grandfather` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(j)(3), am I a caregiver of the minor child` `s 2031 grandfather` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(j)(3), am I a caregiver of the minor child` `s 2031 natural or adoptive parent` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2031(j)(3), am I a caregiver of the minor child` `s 2031 some other relationship` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 2035`
-- A household of 3 with no member on part A assistance may not take part; all 3 on part A: may; 1 of 3 with the Secretary's approval: may; 1 of 3 and approval not decided: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(c), may my household take part in the State's simplified program` 3 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(c), may my household take part in the State's simplified program` 3 3 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(c), may my household take part in the State's simplified program` 3 1 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(c), may my household take part in the State's simplified program` 3 1 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- All 3 on part A: eligible. Only 2 of 3: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(c)(2), is my household eligible to take part in the State's simplified program` 3 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(c)(2), is my household eligible to take part in the State's simplified program` 3 2 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Benefits worked out under SNAP's rules: allowed; under some other source: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(c)(4), may my benefits under the simplified program be worked out under these rules` `s 2035 the supplemental nutrition assistance program` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(c)(4), may my benefits under the simplified program be worked out under these rules` `s 2035 some other source` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Income worked out under the part A program's rules: allowed; under SNAP's rules: not covered by (f)(3)(B).
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(f)(3)(B), may my household's income be worked out under these rules` `s 2035 a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(f)(3)(B), may my household's income be worked out under these rules` `s 2035 the supplemental nutrition assistance program` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Secretary has not determined that no household over 130 percent is eligible for the State program: the text says no. Determined: nothing is granted. Not decided: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(f)(4), may my household get benefits under the simplified program because it is eligible under the State program` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(f)(4), may my household get benefits under the simplified program because it is eligible under the State program` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2035(f)(4), may my household get benefits under the simplified program because it is eligible under the State program` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 2036a`
-- Eligible for SNAP: an eligible individual. Eligible for neither, with the Secretary having determined nothing in the person's favour: the text says no. Not decided: not covered. Eligible for the title 42 benefit while the others are undecided: an eligible individual.
#ASSERT `Under section 2036a(a), am I an eligible individual for nutrition education and obesity prevention` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2036a(a), am I an eligible individual for nutrition education and obesity prevention` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2036a(a), am I an eligible individual for nutrition education and obesity prevention` NOTHING FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2036a(a), am I an eligible individual for nutrition education and obesity prevention` NOTHING TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An eligible individual and a program that promotes healthy choices within the grant: the State agency may offer it. A program outside the grant terms: not covered. Eligibility not decided: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2036a(b), may the State agency offer me its nutrition education and obesity prevention program` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2036a(b), may the State agency offer me its nutrition education and obesity prevention program` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 2036a(b), may the State agency offer me its nutrition education and obesity prevention program` NOTHING FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An applicant, participant or eligible individual, and notifying is practicable: the State agency shall notify. Not practicable: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 2036a(c)(4), must the State agency notify me of the availability of nutrition education and obesity prevention services` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2036a(c)(4), must the State agency notify me of the availability of nutrition education and obesity prevention services` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
